#
# ddl_concurrent_admin_ops (DDL on several tables in shared column families
# running alongside manual compaction, flushes, cancelled compactions,
# drop-index thread wake-ups, ANALYZE, checkpoints and column family drops)
# run under non-default RocksDB background tuning: a single background job,
# subcompactions and bottom-priority compactions, the write buffer manager with
# a small global memtable budget, rate-limited SST file deletion with a short
# obsolete-file period, and a small WAL budget, few open files and a low
# delayed-write rate. See ddl_concurrent_bg_tuning_admin_ops.combinations.
# The write buffer manager combination is in
# compact_lzero_now_concurrent_compaction, disabled until PS-11747 is fixed.
#

# With rocksdb_sst_mgr_rate_bytes_per_sec > 0 the RocksDB delete scheduler also
# handles obsolete WAL files, and RocksDB's own purge sometimes schedules the
# same WAL file twice; the second rename fails because the file is already gone
# and RocksDB logs an error. No data is affected and MyRocks only forwards the
# RocksDB log line, so the message is suppressed here.
--disable_query_log
call mtr.add_suppression("Failed to mark .*[.]log as trash -- IO error: No such file or directory");
--enable_query_log

--let $rounds = 10
--source suite/rocksdb/t/ddl_concurrent_admin_ops.test
